messages:
Maya: quick UX question — the new form action row (primary + dropdown + help link) feels really crowded at smaller widths. attaching screenshot: https://redwood.design/snap/ux-action-row-824.png
Sam: yup, I noticed that on mobile too. options: collapse secondary into kebab, stack vertically, or reduce horizontal padding. :thinking:
Jordan: my vote is split-actions + compact spacing. keep primary visible, group the rest in a menu to reduce visual weight. also we should introduce a component-level spacing token instead of reusing grid tokens.
Liam: accessibility nit — if we go split + menu, keyboard order must be primary -> menu button -> menu items. also use aria-expanded on the menu button and ensure focus returns to the button after close.
Jordan: agreed. quick snippet for the compact token idea:
```css
:root {
  --rwd-spacing-action-compact: 6px; /* new token for action groups */
}
.rwd-split-action {
  display: inline-flex;
  gap: var(--rwd-spacing-action-compact);
}
```
Sam: looks good. question: should we reuse `spacing-compact-2` or create `spacing-action-compact`? creating a dedicated token seems safer for clarity.
Maya: I prefer `spacing-action-compact` as well — makes intent clear for later audits. also noticed a visual overlap: when the action menu animates open the toast that appears from the top overlaps for ~300ms. feels janky.
Liam: lower the toast enter animation to 220ms and make sure we respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. something like:
```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .rwd-toast { transition-duration: 0ms; }
}
.rwd-toast { transition-duration: 220ms; }
```
DesignBot: accessibility scan: the help link color in the action row is failing contrast (ratio 3.2). recommend using `--rwd-text-link` at 4.5:1.
Sam: will prototype split-action + new token + contrast fix on a branch and post screenshots. planning to collapse into kebab at <= 540px.
Maya: awesome, please also add keyboard test cases to the PR description (tab order, menu open/close, focus return). I'll review on staging once it lands. :thumbsup:
Sam: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/rwd-ui/pull/482 — includes token, CSS changes, and a11y notes.
DesignBot: CI queued for rwd-ui#482 — lint and a11y checks running.
Liam: one more tiny thought — when we reduce padding for compact, double-check touch target remains >= 44px for mobile (hit target). if gap reduces, maybe increase hit area via pseudo padding.
Sam: noted. I'll keep hit target and only reduce visual padding inside the control.
Maya: nice. thanks everyone — this should make the action row feel less noisy while staying accessible.
